[{:db/id "q-71270/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" :answer/id #uuid "d138b3b6-10ad-5baa-8d40-161716166c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" :answer/id #uuid "3ce81cc0-c749-5b7b-aae8-7da401f5959e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270/selection/6aa94c810ceb98b13faf6ddb479dbe3124e1f0420de00c874ab0a2533ae53644" :answer/id #uuid "9392e3be-7aa7-5abd-a322-def83c3cac05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270/selection/d9aa6c8d2c61efdd02809872257256325c6ad1aa82d6a94b61940bdd369526d8" :answer/id #uuid "59a70a86-1425-531c-a9b0-57b66d585fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270/selection/c99be99eb9810d179cadcf25a599f896beed484536278a9deca6a9e1fea78495" :answer/id #uuid "a3000ea4-aee3-503f-b65c-4f7d296ec66d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85eebecb-b9cc-579b-ad41-89b7d00bf833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71270/selection/c99be99eb9810d179cadcf25a599f896beed484536278a9deca6a9e1fea78495" :answer-field/choices ["q-71270/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" "q-71270/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" "q-71270/selection/6aa94c810ceb98b13faf6ddb479dbe3124e1f0420de00c874ab0a2533ae53644" "q-71270/selection/d9aa6c8d2c61efdd02809872257256325c6ad1aa82d6a94b61940bdd369526d8" "q-71270/selection/c99be99eb9810d179cadcf25a599f896beed484536278a9deca6a9e1fea78495"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71270" :question/id #uuid "07f0b1a9-ab3f-550e-aed9-fa24adcc5d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-71270" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $y=-2$ and $x=z-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $y=-2$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=z-1$ (or $x-z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a8928978-9199-5d89-85fc-75be4cf1358d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "324cdf96-4124-579b-a770-f0af2947c520" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "78635d73-fef2-5c84-92bf-06f3c8b0a8de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "acc09890-1271-534a-9aa7-ef6465a809ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "100aa6e1-f88f-562d-8158-55ec968a394b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9acc8d8c-164b-5548-ba64-8644a3a2b0f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71464/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-71464/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-71464/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-71464/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-71464/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-71464/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71464" :question/id #uuid "e907b0e4-0542-5071-9a1e-54575ac732d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71464" :question/problem "Given the two planes $y-z=1$ and $2x+z=3$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y-z=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+z=3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and  III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71464/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71464"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection/d55b7c90d2b72c4fc9b287d084a0446ff794b8b02d914e6b47cd067b17af2f36" :answer/id #uuid "49ef3c52-2524-518f-b2f3-1a0a54daaf75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨6,4,-6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection/29eda4358ba9cd6eff315e9cacf44b3714b0650b47da1f0aeae41015b8c4d2f9" :answer/id #uuid "8a8f7a45-4d82-58b9-bd8a-4a39eb05db24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-3,\\,b=⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection/fe232d994d83e4ea061a0273ae8a3c927de1ee9047179c459b8eb6887d39df3c" :answer/id #uuid "b33ba095-c0ae-5126-8eb9-0d3719014ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨6,6,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection/b63615a3a80d5071d02a10ffe3066dfe0a17bfc6cddd14e600ff77e02d193873" :answer/id #uuid "c7782099-a0fd-53c6-86da-c019401e1704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=12,\\,b=⟨6,4,-6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection/fcb06063ffccb89eb2555e89dc8f08addc47f80f4ae0123d5d0594c69e7ed629" :answer/id #uuid "958eab3e-848e-5daa-8090-2f55167ef79a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=6,\\,b=⟨4,6,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "639a9cca-ac75-56eb-870d-145fc313d159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129215/selection/fe232d994d83e4ea061a0273ae8a3c927de1ee9047179c459b8eb6887d39df3c" :answer-field/choices ["q-129215/selection/d55b7c90d2b72c4fc9b287d084a0446ff794b8b02d914e6b47cd067b17af2f36" "q-129215/selection/29eda4358ba9cd6eff315e9cacf44b3714b0650b47da1f0aeae41015b8c4d2f9" "q-129215/selection/fe232d994d83e4ea061a0273ae8a3c927de1ee9047179c459b8eb6887d39df3c" "q-129215/selection/b63615a3a80d5071d02a10ffe3066dfe0a17bfc6cddd14e600ff77e02d193873" "q-129215/selection/fcb06063ffccb89eb2555e89dc8f08addc47f80f4ae0123d5d0594c69e7ed629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129215" :question/id #uuid "583166f3-f984-5b08-b009-d0467651a92a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129215" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $2x-3z=0$ and $2y-3z-6=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n2x-0=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n2y-0-6=0\\,⟹\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨0,3,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,-3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-3⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j+4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨0,3,0⟩+t⟨6,6,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0+3=3,$ and $b=⟨6,6,4⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129215/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129215"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b1ec36b8-e877-5158-9f63-24320f697d1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a5918a05-fcd8-5042-af53-53d9846fbcdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d66d9ffa-275f-5859-b1ba-449c843e4255" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5d743de0-62e6-5fc0-80b4-ce5ef89010b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c3b9f991-4144-574d-b26f-5126b1b33b4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b141f848-4c27-5b0c-bf2a-351e8d6af56b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129241/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-129241/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-129241/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-129241/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-129241/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129241/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129241" :question/id #uuid "959d7c1a-33e8-592b-b5a5-d7f6a288fc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-129241" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+2z=0$ and $x-2y+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129241/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
